{"version":"1","id":"thatdot","handle":"thatdot","name":"thatDot","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/e1b0dfcda2d84af09c522096cb78e212","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":0.5943,"y":0.0864,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":65,"newest_post_at":"2024-04-04T21:40:15.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2022-04-25T07:24:17.724Z","features":{"hype_score":0.015385,"listicle_ratio":0.030769,"question_ratio":0.046154,"avg_read_time":4.630769,"summary_length_avg":323.661538,"title_length_avg":54.169231,"title_length_var":181.986746,"tag_entropy":3.608305,"tag_diversity":0.753846,"top_tag_share":0.076923,"avg_upvotes":0.369231,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.0,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.04,"zero_engagement_share":0.769231,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":0.640309,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.065574},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-6.6029,-7.1029],"cadence_depth":[-2.6176,-3.3088],"hype_variety":[3.5,4.3088],"title_style":[5.2353,6.7647]},"top_tags":[["machine-learning",10],["architecture",10],["kafka",9],["aws",4],["devops",4],["cyber",4],["data-analysis",4],["data-science",4]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Akka to Pekko Migration for thatDot and Quine","Microservice Hell: The State of the Art in Streaming Services","4 Advantages to Streaming Analytics in Graph Form"],"outlier":["Introducing thatDot"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"mEd7nQEAs","title":"Microservice Hell: The State of the Art in Streaming Services","url":"https://www.thatdot.com/blog/microservice-hell-the-state-of-the-art-in-streaming-services","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/microservice-hell-the-state-of-the-art-in-streaming-services-med7nqeas","summary":"The post discusses the state of the art in streaming services, including retrieving data from Apache Kafka, creating a Scala service for printing emitted strings, and implementing event-driven architecture patterns. It introduces thatDot Streaming Graph as a higher-level abstraction for handling scalability and resilience in data pipelines.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/2280c4cdba589d3b9f9cd109a8254fe5?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-04-04T21:40:15.000Z"},{"id":"KtsIG5jgP","title":"4 Advantages to Streaming Analytics in Graph Form","url":"https://www.thatdot.com/blog/4-advantages-to-streaming-analytics-in-graph-form","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/4-advantages-to-streaming-analytics-in-graph-form-ktsig5jgp","summary":"Streaming analytics in graph form offers advantages such as smart filtering, deep relationship analysis, categorical data analysis, and reduced mean time to value.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/e20e763feb4fdc4535742347686cd716?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-03-21T21:21:40.000Z"},{"id":"f0hD3RVJJ","title":"Release Announcement for thatDot Streaming Graph 1.6.1 with ClickHouse Persister","url":"https://www.thatdot.com/blog/release-announcement-for-thatdot-streaming-graph-with-clickhouse-persister","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/release-announcement-for-thatdot-streaming-graph-1-6-1-with-clickhouse-persister-f0hd3rvjj","summary":"thatDot Streaming Graph 1.6.1 has been released with new enhancements including the ability to persist data in ClickHouse and multiple namespaces for better multi-tenant situations.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/6a686422979e69fad6490ca9c90ebfd2?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-03-12T18:56:32.000Z"},{"id":"k7GTdr4pp","title":"Akka to Pekko Migration for thatDot and Quine","url":"https://www.thatdot.com/blog/akka-to-pekko-migration-for-thatdot-and-quine","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/akka-to-pekko-migration-for-thatdot-and-quine-k7gtdr4pp","summary":"Akka changed its license to a commercial license, causing implications for users. thatDot migrated to Pekko as an open source alternative, modifying their code and replacing dependencies.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/4d6b175c69fb81e7ab21827190ee8b76?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":5,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-02-22T17:10:48.000Z"},{"id":"X33KdOhJT","title":"Data Exfiltration Detection in AWS CloudTrail Logs Using Categorical Data","url":"https://www.thatdot.com/blog/identifying-data-exfiltration-in-aws-cloudtrail-logs-using-categorical-anomaly-detection","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/data-exfiltration-detection-in-aws-cloudtrail-logs-using-categorical-data-x33kdohjt","summary":"The article discusses the use of categorical anomaly detection in AWS CloudTrail logs to identify data exfiltration. It explains the challenges of detecting data exfiltration and how graph-based techniques can help prevent it. It also highlights the role of thatDot Novelty Detector in detecting and categorizing novel behaviors.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/05256301bd02f21db1fdf50c25d6c5c8?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-24T17:44:08.000Z"},{"id":"IMUwnwOqU","title":"Network Log Analysis Using Categorical Anomaly Detection","url":"https://www.thatdot.com/blog/network-log-analysis-using-categorical-anomaly-detection","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/network-log-analysis-using-categorical-anomaly-detection-imuwnwoqu","summary":"Network log analysis using categorical anomaly detection provides insight into communication behaviors between logical hosts by analyzing network connection summary records. The analysis includes metrics such as bandwidth and categorical elements like IP addresses and connection state. The resulting visualization can identify abnormal behavior and can be used for DDoS detection, host communication analysis, and new protocol discovery. thatDot Novelty Detector is a useful tool for enriching telemetry data and enabling real-time anomaly detection.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/113f6fe0181feb5e402ea3c16d6aac05?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-24T17:44:08.000Z"},{"id":"7bGGfiyaR","title":"AWS Names thatDot's Novelty Detector As A Containers Anywhere Partner","url":"https://www.thatdot.com/blog/aws-announces-thatdot-anomaly-detector-as-a-containers-anywhere-launch-partner","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/aws-names-thatdot-s-novelty-detector-as-a-containers-anywhere-partner-7bggfiyar","summary":"AWS has named thatDot's Novelty Detector as a partner for Containers Anywhere, making it easier to bring cloud-based data management into enterprise data centers. The Novelty Detector uses categorical data to identify anomalies and provide actionable insights.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1d71cd672e4cdd2a503a8a015ee3ba7f?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-24T17:44:08.000Z"},{"id":"nSEhHPL2b","title":"New to Quine's Novelty Detector: Visualizations and Enhancements","url":"https://www.thatdot.com/blog/thatdot-anomaly-detector-enhancements-visualizations-and-data-transformations","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/new-to-quine-s-novelty-detector-visualizations-and-enhancements-nsehhpl2b","summary":"thatDot has added data exploration capabilities and data transformation functions to their Novelty Detector for Categorical data. The new features include Data Distribution Plots for visualizing score distribution and Observation Detail Visualizations for understanding the root cause of a score. Additionally, users can now define data transformations using javascript to experiment and refine their anomaly detection efforts.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/530f6f0e6fa7a38102ef7b92458fff46?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-24T17:44:08.000Z"},{"id":"UKypp0KYq","title":"Draw Connections to Build Insights","url":"https://www.thatdot.com/blog/draw-connections-to-build-insights","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/draw-connections-to-build-insights-ukypp0kyq","summary":"Drawing connections between data in a graph structure allows for better data analysis and streaming computation. JSON objects can be treated as nodes in a graph, with key-value pairs becoming properties on the nodes. Semantic caching can be used with iterative processing on native graphs to optimize computation. Overall, drawing connections in data is a powerful way to answer human-level questions with context.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/39f6dfb8a37d06f688e78123463019e0?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-24T17:44:08.000Z"},{"id":"RVoxo8pij","title":"The Three D\u2019s of Graph Data","url":"https://www.thatdot.com/blog/3d-data","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-three-d-s-of-graph-data-rvoxo8pij","summary":"Data comes from one source and when used to understand a complex system, it becomes grossly distorted. Building a 3D model of the system's data allows for a better understanding. The three main principles for building 3D data are drawing connections between data, defining new levels of data, and drilling down to answer questions. thatDot's mission is to turn high-volume data into high-value data.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/eb3593b52cf33371bd47d18a2bb0a686?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-10-24T17:44:08.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["bignerdranch","getambassador","beambloggers","fgiesen","coralogix"],"opposite_handles":["dailydevworld","on_leuwcq","horde","watercooler","dotnetsquad"],"similar":[{"id":"bignerdranch","handle":"bignerdranch","name":"Big Nerd Ranch","is_squad":false,"x":0.4782,"y":0.0364,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":21,"image":"https://me